hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"285","On the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Umm Qais The daughter of Muhsan Al-Asadiya, she said: “I entered the house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a young son of mine who did not eat food, so he urinated on him and poured water on him.” He brushed it"
"286","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Umm Qais bint Muhsin Al-Asadiya, that she brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a young son of hers who did not eat. food, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made him sit on his lap, and he urinated on it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for water and sprinkled it. And he did not wash it.” Yunus once called me, saying: Ibn Wahb told me, Malik, Al-Layth, Amr bin Al-Harith, and Yunus told me that Ibn Shihab narrated to them, with something like it, both in the chain of transmission and in the text."
